  "live_records": {
    "q-103171": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103171",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(2,8)=2.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 2\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
