    "q-213273": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213273",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that $8a≡8b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ construct a statement that also must be true:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}a≡{{field-2}}b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,{{field-3}})\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a common factor of $k=2,$ and the congruence can be written as\n\n$$\n2\\cdot 4a≡2\\cdot 4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can cancel out the common factor on both sides of the congruence and the modulus:\n\n$$\n\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4a≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
