    "q-213297": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213297",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ 5\\cdot a & ≡5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{5}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{5}\\cdot 3) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\n.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213297-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only\n"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213297-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II only",
              "html": "II only\n"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213297-c",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "III only",
              "html": "III only"
            },
