    "q-77149": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77149",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Given that $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\n- $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a & ≡6b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4) \\\\ 3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(3,4)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77149-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "html": "I and II only"
            },
